  "id": "COMPOUND:9422 - PROTEIN:6295",
  "verbalization": "Tepoxalin is implicated in the biological pathway leading to Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 7 through a series of molecular interactions. The drug targets Dipeptidyl peptidase IX, which in turn is a target of another compound, 5-(2,5-DICHLOROPHENYL)-2-FUROIC ACID. This second compound, in turn, has a target that is part of the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family. The evidence suggests a chain of targets, where Tepoxalin's activity may influence the downstream pathway through Dipeptidyl peptidase IX, potentially modulating the activity of the Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 7. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Tepoxalin in regulating the activity of this enzyme family, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
